        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.45 g, 1 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (20 mL), then triethanolamine (0.13 mL, 1 mmol), 6-chloro-2-hydroxypyridine (0.12 g, 1 mmol) and triethylamine (0.3 mL, 2 mmol) were added. The colorless solution was stirred for 6 h, any precipitate was filtered, and the filtrate was allowed to evaporate slowly. Colorless block crystals of 1 formed within 2–3 days. The central carbonate is derived from atmospheric CO2 rather than an added carbonate reagent.",
